et policy gives 2 years, which beats the asymmetric mix at 2.5 expected and the both-send case at 4 in the joint sense. The asymmetric policy only works if I condition on being Sasha, and that would break the single shared function, so I'm setting that aside.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying the P-FDT framework here: two copies of the same function run on different inputs, with a shared policy node that maps observations to actions. Both instances read that policy, so the joint optimum is quiet on both inputs for two years each, versus four years if both send. I'm now checking the mixed case, where one input triggers send and the other stays quiet, which gives me zero utility.\n\nI'm weighing whether the policy can be chosen with the shared prior, since I don't know which input I'll receive. Under that symmetric prior, the quiet-quiet policy gives 2 years, which beats the asymmetric mix at 2.5 expected and the both-send case at 4 in the joint sense. The asymmetric policy only works if I condition on being Sasha, and that would break the single shared function, so I'm setting that aside.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9784,"completion_tokens":876,"total_tokens":10660,"cost":0.056656,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.056656,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039136,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01752},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":518,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}